CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* char32_t through a converting constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* char16_t and wchar_t: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* char32_t promotes to unsigned int: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* char16_t, wchar_t promote to int: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Assumes the x86-64 Linux data model (32-bit signed wchar_t).  g++ 13
(-fsanitize=address,undefined) and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
